---
description: Start every new feature on its own Git branch
alwaysApply: true
---

# Feature branches

- Create a descriptive feature branch before implementing any new feature, even if the user does not mention branching.
- Inspect and preserve existing work; prefer an up-to-date main as the base when appropriate.
- Keep follow-up work for an existing feature on that feature's branch.
- Do not commit, push, or merge unless the user requests it.
